49. Circuit breaker vs bulkhead
This distinction is extremely important.
Suppose B is slow.
Without protection:
1000 requests
   |
   v
1000 threads waiting for B
Eventually:
thread pool exhausted
A circuit breaker might eventually open.
But before enough failures accumulate, you can already have resource exhaustion.
A bulkhead limits concurrent calls:
maximum 50 calls to B
So:
1000 incoming requests
        |
        v
   +---------+
   | 50 slots|
   +---------+
        |
        v
        B
The remaining requests are rejected or queued according to policy.
Circuit breaker:
“B is unhealthy.”
Bulkhead:
“Regardless of B's health, I refuse to let B consume more than this amount of my resources.”
Different mechanisms.
________________________________________
