Lesson 4 — Circuit Breaker + Retry + Timeout + Bulkhead as One System
This is where system design becomes much more interesting.
A common mistake is to learn these as four independent patterns:
Timeout
Retry
Circuit Breaker
Bulkhead
and then configure each one separately.
In production, that is dangerous.
They form a coupled control system.
A bad configuration can turn:
one slow dependency
into:
