63. Sliding window + timeout interaction
Suppose:
window = 10 sec
and timeout:
2 sec
A request that hangs for 2 seconds doesn't produce an outcome until then.
Therefore failure detection isn't instantaneous.
If 100 requests all begin hanging at:
T=0
their failures may only become visible around:
T=2 sec
So your breaker may take at least roughly the timeout duration to observe those failures.
This is why:
Circuit-breaker detection latency is constrained by outcome latency.
A circuit breaker cannot count a timeout until the timeout actually occurs.
