You receive:
20 requests
All fail due to a transient error.
Then each retries.
If retry is poorly designed, those retries compete for the same capacity.
Conceptually:
20 original
   ↓
fail
   ↓
20 retries
   ↓
fail
   ↓
20 more retries
Bulkhead says:
"Regardless of retry behavior, Payment cannot consume unlimited resources."
Circuit Breaker says:
"If failures become persistent, stop making calls."
Timeout says:
"Don't let one operation wait forever."
So now you're seeing the architecture as a system of controls, rather than isolated patterns.
