22. But here's an advanced problem: reserved capacity can be wasteful
Suppose:
Payment = 20 slots
Search = 60 slots
but currently:
Payment traffic = 0
Search traffic = huge
You might have:
Payment:
20 unused

Search:
60 exhausted
So strict isolation can sacrifice utilization.
This creates a fundamental distributed-system tradeoff:
Isolation  ←────────────→  Utilization
More isolation:
+ better failure containment
- potentially lower resource utilization
More sharing:
+ better utilization
- greater risk of noisy-neighbor failures
There is no universal "correct" number.
This is why Bulkhead configuration is an architecture/capacity-planning problem, not a magic library setting.
