31. Where should rate limiting live?
This is a common interview question.
There isn't one universal answer.
At CDN/WAF
Good for:
DDoS
IP-based abuse
very cheap rejection
At API Gateway
Good for:
API key
tenant
endpoint
authentication-aware quotas
Inside application
Good for:
business-specific limits
resource-aware costs
fine-grained policies
At downstream client
Good for:
external API quotas
database protection
dependency-specific limits
A mature system may use all of them, but for different purposes.
