4. The mathematical operation
When a request arrives at time now:
elapsed = now - lastRefill
Then:
refilledTokens =
    elapsed × refillRate
And:
tokens =
    min(capacity,
        oldTokens + refilledTokens)
Then if:
tokens >= requestedCost
consume:
tokens -= requestedCost
Otherwise reject.
The important point:
We don't need a background thread continuously adding tokens.
This is a common misunderstanding.
________________________________________
5. Lazy refill
Suppose:
capacity = 100
refillRate = 10/sec
At:
t = 0
tokens = 0
Nobody sends requests for 5 seconds.
Do we need a scheduler to add:
10
20
30
40
50
every second?
No.
When the next request arrives at:
t = 5 sec
we calculate:
0 + (5 × 10)
= 50
and continue.
This is called lazy refill.
It saves enormous amounts of unnecessary work.
