Suppose Redis fails.
Architecture:
                 Redis
                /     \
             UP        DOWN
             |           |
             v           v
         distributed    local
           bucket       bucket
The local fallback provides approximate protection.
But you should monitor that state:
rate_limiter_redis_failure_total
rate_limiter_fallback_total
If fallback mode lasts for 30 minutes, that's not normal operation.
It is an incident.
________________________________________
29. Redis timeout
Don't let:
redisLimiter.tryAcquire(...)
hang indefinitely.
Configure a short timeout appropriate to your latency budget.
Think:
API timeout = 500 ms
You cannot reasonably have:
Redis limiter timeout = 2 sec
because the limiter can outlive the request itself.
The limiter's timeout must fit inside the request's overall latency budget.
